+# The delete-then-insert keeps exactly one ACCEPT per CIDR across the retry
+# loop, ordered ahead of the default DROP; the loop re-asserts the permits
+# because EOS (re)programs its firewall chains during boot.
+#
+# NOTE: the return-PATH is no longer handled here. When the CR maps eth0 to an
+# EOS management interface, EOS owns eth0's address and routes end to end: the
+# startup-config-seed init container materializes the pod IP and interface
